# Clean Code

## Constants over magic numbers

- Replace hard-coded values with named constants when meaning is not obvious.
- Use descriptive names; keep constants at module top or in a dedicated constants module.

## Meaningful names

- Names should reveal purpose and usage; avoid unclear abbreviations.

## Comments

- Prefer self-documenting code; comment the *why*, not the obvious *what*.
- Document non-obvious behavior, APIs, and side effects.

## Single responsibility

- Functions do one thing; split when logic branches or mixes concerns.

## DRY

- Extract repeated logic; maintain single sources of truth.

## Structure and encapsulation

- Keep related code together; extract nested conditionals into well-named helpers.

## Maintenance

- Refactor within scope; leave touched code cleaner than you found it.

## Testing

- Add tests when requested or when they add meaningful coverage.
- Cover edge cases and error paths when writing tests.
